[ext_resource type="Texture2D" path="res://assets/bonelight/ui/spells/windfall-grass.png" id="3_icon"]

; Windfall (scripts/Windfall.cs), 2026-11-09: a small iron-fruited tree planted where the wizard stands, whose fruit ripens
; one at a time. An enemy bumping it brings one ripe fruit down on itself; the wizard walking back under it brings the whole
; crop down in a ring round it. Grass + Metal: the living wood and the iron. Nobody's opener; everyone earns it with the
; Fieldfare feat (Grass and Metal kills in one run). TargetingMode 9 is Planted - where he stands, paid out when shaken - and
; DamageShape 3 a burst over an area (each fruit thuds on everything near where it lands).
;
; BaseDamage is ONE FRUIT'S THUD on each body it reaches. BaseCooldown is the planting (the ONE fire loop); a cast beside one
; of his own trees waits, ripe, for him to step clear. BaseProjectileCount is the TREES that may stand at once (plus Amount,
; Kindled Ward's ceiling): at the cap a planting uproots the oldest, which drops what it holds where it stood. The crop a
; tree ripens is Windfall.BaseCrop (3) plus the Crop lines here (Effect 23, "Fruit +1" on the card); a fruit ripens every
; Windfall.RipenSeconds (1.6 s) at the wizard's own cast speed.
;
; FIRST GUESSES, untuned. Spells start small (Eric, 2026-11-02): one tree and three fruit at level 1, two trees at 3, three
; at 6; a crop of four at 2, five at 5, six at 7. Written out in full so Player.EnsureRelevantLevelUps generates nothing of
; its own (ScalingTagsMask 19: Damage, Cooldown, ProjectileCount): every level adds damage and even levels shorten the
; planting by 0.2 s. Level 8: 35 a fruit, three trees, six fruit each, a planting every 6.2 s - so each tree stands about
; 19 s before it is the oldest, and fills in under 10.

